                "id": "o4om8urmtcmtha4",
                "text": "Buffers Summary"
              }
            ],
            "id": "kjt1ks6pqzt85it",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "A solution containing a mixture of a weak acid and its conjugate base, or of a weak base and its conjugate acid, is called a buffer solution. The presence of a weak conjugate acid-base pair provides reactants that may neutralize small additions of strong acid or base, yielding weaker conjugate partners. The hydronium ion concentration of a buffer solution therefore does not change significantly when a small amount of acid or base is added."
              }
            ],
